DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nJoin us to launch Aaron Rabinowitz’s debut bo
 ok of poetry\,\nSuggestions\,\nwith guest reader Damian Rogers.\nAaron Rab
 inowitz's writing appears in journals such as G\nrain\, The Southern Revie
 w\, Copper Nickel\, Longreads\, EPOCH\, Prairie Schooner\,\nand\nThe Malah
 at Review\,\nand has been cited as a Best American Essays Notable. He is t
 he winner of PRISM international’s Creative Nonfiction Contest and the M
 eridian Short Prose Prize. He has been a writer-in-residence at The Banff 
 Centre\, the Deer Lake Artist Residencies\, PLAYA\, and elsewhere.\nSugges
 tions\n(Gaspereau Press) is his debut collection of poetry.  Aaron also w
 ill water your plants when you are out of town. IG: @anotheraaronrabinowit
 z\nDamian J. Rogers is the author of the concisely titled memoir A\nN ALPH
 ABET FOR JOANNA: A PORTRAIT OF MY MOTHER IN 26 FRAGMENTS (\nKnopfCanada)\,
  about a relationship shadowed by trauma and illness. She has also publish
 ed two poetry collections:\nDear Leader\n(Coach House Books)\, which was n
 ominated for the Trillium Poetry Prize\; and Paper Radio (ECW Press)\, whi
 ch was nominated for the Pat Lowther Memorial Award and the ReLit Award. S
 he currently teaches creative writing at Toronto Metropolitan University a
 nd in private workshops. She also practices\, writes about\, and teaches T
 arot. IG: @dam.rogers
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
