BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR OUR AUGUST FICTION BOOK CLUB:
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T203000
UID:bm-5886520260817@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/August_Fi
 c_Book_Club_26.jpg?cb=1784399271
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nJoin us for a discussion of the novel\,\nTranscri
 ption\nby Ben Lerner.\nBen Lerner is back with a lightning flash of a nove
 l that is at once a gripping emotional drama and a brilliant examination o
 f the devices\, digital and literary\, we use to store—or to erase—our
  memories.\nThe narrator is to conduct an interview with Thomas\, his nine
 ty-year-old mentor and the father of his friend\, Max\, but he drops his s
 martphone in the hotel sink. He arrives at Thomas’ house with no recordi
 ng device\, a fact he is mysteriously unable to confess.\nWhat unfolds fro
 m this dreamlike circumstance is both the unforgettable story of the trian
 gle formed by Thomas\, Max\, and the narrator\, and a brilliant meditation
  on those technologies that enrich or impoverish our connection to one ano
 ther\, that store or obliterate memory. Utterly contemporary\, Lerner comb
 ines trenchant insight with lyric mystery. Ultimately\, Transcription demo
 nstrates what only a work of fiction can record.\nJoin us on Monday\, Augu
 st 17th and Tuesday\, August 18th for a thrilling conversation. We hope to
  see you there.\nYour book club ticket includes:\nA glass of wine (or anot
 her beverage of your choice).\nA thoughtful conversation with our brillian
 t moderator\, Lee Suksi.\nA $20 credit toward any book in the shop *\nGET 
 YOUR TICKETS HERE!\nA few details:\nTicket price includes HST and fees.\n*
 $20 book credit is valid on the night of attendance only (non-refundable a
 nd non-transferable).\nWine is served on the night of the event (ID requir
 ed).\nTickets are non-refundable within 7 days of the event\; due to limit
 ed capacity and planning\, we’re not able to transfer tickets to future 
 book club sessions.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:MAKE IT MAKE SENSE: THE FLYING BOOKS NONFICTION BOOKCLUB
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T203000
UID:bm-6051920260929@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Trash_Sep
 t_2026_Nonfic.jpg?cb=1786046275
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nJoin Tomas Hachard\, author of\nCity in Flames\n\
 , on Tuesday\, September 29th\, from 6:30 to 8:30 pm for a lively discussi
 on of\nTrash\nby Simon Paré-Poupart.\nA Montreal garbageman's sharp and f
 unny memoir/exposé\, in which he attempts to convince people to "stop ima
 gining that your garbage magically disappears" . . .\nThis fascinating no-
 bullshit account of twenty years in waste management paints a vivid portra
 it of the heroic labor\, anarchic spirit\, and violent conditions of the p
 eople who keep our cities clean.\nParé-Poupart’s story is atypical: he 
 started working as a garbageman to pay for school\, and after earning grad
 uate degrees and working in more “respectable” fields\, he is still on
  a truck — out of love for the physical rush\, for his rough-and-tumble 
 colleagues\, and for an honesty and freedom that no other job has yet give
 n him.\nJoin us on Tuesday\, Septemeber 29th. We hope to see you there.\nG
 ET YOUR TICKETS HERE!\nYour book club ticket includes:\nA glass of wine (o
 r another beverage of your choice).\nA thoughtful conversation with Tomas 
 Hachard\, author of\nCity in Flames\n.\nA $20 credit toward any book in th
 e shop.\nA few details:\nTicket price includes HST and fees.\n$20 book cre
 dit is valid on the night of attendance only (non-refundable and non-trans
 ferable).\nWine is served on the night of the event (ID required).\nTicket
 s are non-refundable within 7 days of the event\; due to limited capacity 
 and planning\, we’re not able to transfer tickets to future book club se
 ssions.
LOCATION:Flying Books at Neverland\, 371 Queen St. W.
